// User-approved shared experience and explicit scientific model scope.
"science.scope" = "Linear global-mean temperature anomaly model; an eight-year teaching scenario, not an absolute-temperature or regional climate forecast.";
"science.model" = "C dΔT/dt = F − λΔT; F = 340 m(1−a) − 238 + 3.7 log₂(CO₂/C₀) W/m². For constant parameters: ΔT(t) = (F/λ)[1 − exp(−λt/C)]. The balanced reference has ΔT=0, ASR=OLR=238 W/m². Live energy output is evaluated at the observed day, not the terminal forecast.";
"science.units" = "ΔT is an anomaly in kelvin (the same numerical difference in °C), not absolute °C. λ>0 is restoring radiative damping in W/(m² K). C=6,10,18 W y/(m² K); one model year=365 days=31,536,000 s. C_SI=C×31,536,000 J/(m² K). Positive N=ASR−OLR warms the reservoir; dΔQ/dt_seconds=N.";
"science.coefficient" = "3.7 W/m² per CO₂ doubling is the original rounded logarithmic teaching coefficient (5.35 ln2≈3.71 in the older IPCC approximation). It is not the AR6 effective forcing estimate (3.93±0.47 W/m²), a measured forecast, or a full climate-feedback calculation. No clouds, spatial transport, variable forcing or multi-layer ocean are solved.";
"science.colors" = "Orange solid curve: scenario anomaly; gray dashed curve: balanced reference, on one shared temperature axis. SW orange solid arrow and LW purple dashed arrow are schematic energy flows, with lengths proportional to current flux. Thermal infrared is invisible; purple does not represent its real visible color. EBM circle denotes a global-mean reservoir.";
"science.endpoint" = "The animation reveals one finite 2,920-day record and stops once at its endpoint; climate evolution is not claimed to end there. Pause/resume preserves the presentation phase. Changing a physical parameter starts a new scenario at ΔT=0; it is not an intervention on the existing reservoir. Backgrounding pauses; returning requires resume.";
"science.interaction" = "Two fingers observe the stage at 1–3× without changing climate parameters or time. One finger on the chart selects a previously revealed day for inspection. It never advances the simulation or changes forcing. Interrupted gestures and window changes roll back unfinished probes. This reservoir has no draggable physical apparatus.";
"science.capacityPreset" = "Compared with the CO₂-doubled preset, this preset keeps CO₂/C₀=2 and increases C from 10 to 18 W y/(m² K). The equilibrium anomaly is unchanged; the response time increases.";
